-4|0@Minneapolis^1438542187#ctp3l1d:horatiorincewind$:The guy lecturing some stranger about what he thinks she may or may not have purchased? Yeah, that's actually the epitome of trolling. It's shit that people do to lecture and belittle the poor all the time. He doesn't know anything about this woman other than the limited sliver in this article. There are numerous issues that go into people driving without a license or insurance. This woman could have had who knows how man factor into her case? This article highlights some of the background on this, http://www.startribune.com/in-minneapolis-minor-traffic-violations-spiral-into-major-problems/305265551/ As well, I can't find it but there is a good story about the influence of court fees that are applied to most tickets and fines in the State of Minnesota. Due to the state legislature's inability to fund the court system sustainably they have to make up the revenue they need to operate off of fees placed on the smallest of crimes. Often times these fees are more than the costs of the tickets or the fines. This creates a cycle which makes it harder and harder for poor people to work within. 
