1|0@Minneapolis^1438955891#cturuuy:Bukakke-Sake$:Yeah after living in texas for awhile I have to say, Minnesota in general is much more ticket happy. They also make it almost impossible to fight a ticket. Texas is much different. I think I know why too. Minnesota has big bills. Lots of programs, lots of bike trails, a huge amount of public sector staff. And it all costs money, alot of money. People don't want any more rises to their already high taxes and the public sector refuses to make any cuts so they need alternative revenue streams. Tickets are a big one. I have a friend who just got a job doing IT for the city. He started off day 1 with 24 personal days to take off in addition to his 58000 a year doing desktop support. I have seen this level of compensation for his position in few other places.
